     3,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\">Dear Stan users, <br>I have a regression model that works with one subject, but I’d like to make it a multilevel model - the data consist of repeated observations nested within subjects. Below is a simplified, made-up example to illustrate the issue. There is a dependent and an independent variable and I’d like to estimate a number of intercepts and slopes that depends on the number of conditions (one or more). In the example below we are estimating two intercepts (alpha) and one slope (beta). <br><br>As you can see, the example below ignores that there is more than one subject. What is the best way to turn it in a multilevel model (random intercepts and slopes model)? I think the intuitive way to do it would be indexing alpha and beta for subjects, eg, alpha[subj[n]], but I’m already indexing alpha and beta for conditions. Is there any way I can use two indices so to estimate alpha and beta for each subject and condition? Or can I just add a random intercept term to the equation? Any other solution? Any difference in therm of efficiency? <br><br>Thank you for any suggestion or comment you may have. <br>Best, <br>Luca<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># ------------------------------------------------------------------------------.</span><span><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Dependent variable</span><span><br>y </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">4</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">5</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">7</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">7</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">9</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">8</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">10</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">11</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">12</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">14</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span><br>       </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">4</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">5</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">5</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">6</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">8</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">9</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">9</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Independent variable</span><span><br>x </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">4</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">5</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">6</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">7</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">8</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">9</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">10</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span><br>       </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">4</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">5</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">6</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">7</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">8</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">9</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">10</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Conditions (One or more; In this example 2 conditions for alpha and 1 for beta)</span><span><br>cond_alpha </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span>  </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># conditions for subj 1</span><span><br>                </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span>  </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># conditions for subj 2</span><span><br><br>cond_beta </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span>   </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># conditions for subj 1</span><span><br>               </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span>   </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># conditions for subj 2</span><span><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># subjects</span><span><br>subj </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># subject 1</span><span><br>          </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># subject 2</span><span><br><br>n_alpha </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span> length</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>unique</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>cond_alpha</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># number of conditions for alpha</span><span><br>n_beta </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span> length</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>unique</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>cond_beta</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span>   </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># number of conditions for beta</span><span><br><br>J </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span> length</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>unique</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>subj</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span>  </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># number of subjects</span><span><br>N </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span> length</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># number of observations</span><span><br><br><br>plot</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> col</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span>ifelse</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>subj</span><span style=\"color:#660\">==</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;red&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;blue&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span><br><br><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Stan model</span><span><br>smodel </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;<br>data {<br>    int&lt;lower=1&gt; N;    // number of observations<br>    vector[N] x;       // predictor vector<br>    vector[N] y;       // outcome vector<br><br>    // conditions<br>    int cond_alpha[N]; <br>    int cond_beta[N];  <br><br>    int&lt;lower=1&gt; n_alpha; <br>    int&lt;lower=1&gt; n_beta; <br>}<br>parameters {<br>    vector&lt;lower = -15, upper = 20&gt;[n_alpha] alpha;  // alpha<br>    vector&lt;lower =  -5, upper = 20&gt;[n_beta] beta;    // beta<br>    real&lt;lower=0&gt; sigma;    // error<br>}<br>transformed parameters {<br>    vector[N] mu;<br>    // model <br>    for (n in 1:N)<br>        mu[n] = alpha[cond_alpha[n]] + beta[cond_beta[n]] * x[n]; <br>}<br>model {<br>    // priors<br>    alpha ~ uniform(-15,20); <br>    beta ~ uniform(-5,20); <br>    sigma ~ cauchy(0,5);<br><br>    // likelihood<br>    y ~ normal(mu, sigma); <br>}<br>&quot;</span><span><br><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># fit model</span><span><br>fit </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span> stan</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>model_code </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span> smodel</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> iter </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">5000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> chains </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span><br></span><span style=\"color:#008\">print</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>fit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># ------------------------------------------------------------------------------.</span><span><br><br></span></div></code></div><br><br><br><br></div><div><br></div></div></blockquote></div></div></div>"
